{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Every place where the sole of your foot treads shall be yours, from the wilderness, etc.</b> — According to the opinion of our Sages, these are two promises: that every place they wish to conquer in the land of Shinar and the land of Assyria and elsewhere shall be theirs, and all the commandments apply therein, for it is all the land of Israel; and from the wilderness and the Lebanon to the western sea shall be your boundary, which you are obligated to conquer and to destroy the nations from there, as it says here (Deuteronomy 11:23), \"And you shall dispossess nations greater and mightier than yourselves,\" and to uproot idolatry and its attendants, as He mentioned above (Deuteronomy 7:5, 25), and He promised that no man shall stand before you — whether in the land mentioned or in every place where the sole of your foot treads. From here our Sages derived (tractate Challah 4:7) the dispute regarding Syria, which they call an individual's conquest, the reason being that David conquered it of his own volition, without inquiring through the Urim and Thummim and without consulting the Sanhedrin, for he was obligated first to dispossess all seven nations and only afterward, if he wished, to go to another land, as HaShem promised here; and because that conquest was not carried out according to the ordinance of the Torah, some of them said: its name is not conquest, and its law regarding commandments is like the law of outside the land, and so it is taught in the Sifre (Eikev 24). And some of them say in the Talmud (Avodah Zarah 21a): its name is conquest, for even though it was not done in the prescribed order, since he went there and conquered it, the verse was fulfilled in him — \"it shall be yours,\" and it is the land of Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The citation (ז ה כה) refers to Deuteronomy 7:5 and 7:25, rendered here as (Deuteronomy 7:5, 25)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:48:12.321452039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}